# Design Document: Hermes MCP Lab

## Overview

Hermes MCP Lab is a new top-level subsystem layered on top of the existing Hermes backend. It adds an experiment execution engine, MCP version registry, evaluation pipeline, regression detector, and a dedicated Lab UI — without modifying the existing chat, replay, or session subsystems.

The design reuses Hermes's existing primitives:
- `EventStore` / `EventBus` for trace recording (append-only, WAL SQLite)
- `LLMEngine` for model routing (via `LiteLLM`)
- `MCPClientManager` for live MCP server connectivity
- `WorkbenchBridge` (FastAPI) for the HTTP/WebSocket API layer

New Lab tables are added to the same SQLite database via `LabStore`, a dedicated store class that owns all DDL for Lab entities. The existing `events` and `sessions` tables are not touched.

---

## Architecture

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Tauri Desktop Shell                     │
│  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  Chat UI     │  │         Lab UI (new)              │   │
│  │  (existing)  │  │  Dataset Mgr · Experiment Builder │   │
│  │              │  │  Run Monitor · Dashboard · Diff   │   │
│  └──────┬───────┘  └───────────────┬──────────────────┘   │
└─────────┼──────────────────────────┼────────────────────── ┘
          │  WebSocket/HTTP          │  HTTP + SSE
          ▼                          ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   WorkbenchBridge (FastAPI)                 │
│  /api/...  (existing)    /api/lab/...  (new)                │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
          │                          │
          ▼                          ▼
┌──────────────────┐    ┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Existing Core   │    │           Lab Core (new)           │
│  EventStore      │    │  LabStore (SQLite, same DB)        │
│  EventBus        │    │  DatasetManager                    │
│  LLMEngine       │◄───│  MatrixEngine                      │
│  MCPClientMgr    │◄───│  RunExecutor                       │
│  ReplayEngine    │    │  EvaluationEngine                  │
│  SessionStore    │    │  RegressionDetector                │
└──────────────────┘    │  MockMCPServer                     │
                        │  LabBridge (API router)            │
                        └────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Directory Layout

New files added to the repo (no existing files modified initially):

```
lab/
  __init__.py
  store.py           # LabStore — all DDL + SQL for Lab tables
  dataset.py         # DatasetManager
  registry.py        # MCPVersionRegistry
  matrix.py          # MatrixEngine
  executor.py        # RunExecutor
  evaluation.py      # EvaluationEngine
  regression.py      # RegressionDetector
  mock_mcp.py        # MockMCPServer
  bridge.py          # LabBridge — FastAPI router mounted on /api/lab
  models.py          # Pydantic models for Lab entities
```

`ui/bridge.py` gains one line to mount the `LabBridge` router.

---

## Data Model

### New SQLite Tables (managed by `LabStore`)

All tables live in the existing `.hermes/hermes.db` file. Foreign keys are enforced (WAL + `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON` already active).

```sql
-- Datasets (versioned, immutable versions)
CREATE TABLE lab_datasets (
    dataset_id   TEXT NOT NULL,
    version      INTEGER NOT NULL,
    name         TEXT NOT NULL,
    description  TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
    created_at   TEXT NOT NULL,
    PRIMARY KEY (dataset_id, version)
);

-- Tasks within a dataset version
CREATE TABLE lab_tasks (
    task_id             TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    dataset_id          TEXT NOT NULL,
    dataset_version     INTEGER NOT NULL,
    prompt              TEXT NOT NULL,
    expected_tool_calls BLOB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',   -- JSON array of tool names
    expected_assertions BLOB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',   -- JSON array of assertion strings
    FOREIGN KEY (dataset_id, dataset_version)
        REFERENCES lab_datasets(dataset_id, version)
);

-- MCP server version registrations
CREATE TABLE lab_mcp_versions (
    mcp_version_id      TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    name                TEXT NOT NULL,
    version_tag         TEXT NOT NULL,
    transport           TEXT NOT NULL,   -- 'stdio' | 'sse'
    connection_config   BLOB NOT NULL,   -- JSON
    schema_snapshot     BLOB NOT NULL,   -- JSON, captured at registration
    registered_at       TEXT NOT NULL,
    UNIQUE (name, version_tag)
);

-- Tool description variants
CREATE TABLE lab_tool_variants (
    variant_id      TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    mcp_version_id  TEXT NOT NULL,
    tool_name       TEXT NOT NULL,
    description     TEXT NOT NULL,
    input_schema    BLOB,               -- JSON override, nullable
    created_at      TEXT NOT NULL,
    FOREIGN KEY (mcp_version_id) REFERENCES lab_mcp_versions(mcp_version_id)
);

-- Model configurations
CREATE TABLE lab_model_configs (
    model_config_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    name            TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    provider        TEXT NOT NULL,
    model           TEXT NOT NULL,
    temperature     REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.0,
    max_tokens      INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 4096,
    system_prompt   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
    api_key_env     TEXT,
    api_base        TEXT,
    created_at      TEXT NOT NULL
);

-- Workflow configurations
CREATE TABLE lab_workflow_configs (
    workflow_config_id  TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    name                TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    system_prompt       TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
    max_turns           INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 6,
    timeout_seconds     REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 120.0,
    created_at          TEXT NOT NULL
);

-- Experiments (matrix definition)
CREATE TABLE lab_experiments (
    experiment_id   TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    name            TEXT NOT NULL,
    status          TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',  -- pending|running|completed|cancelled
    created_at      TEXT NOT NULL,
    completed_at    TEXT
);

-- Links between experiment and its variant selections
CREATE TABLE lab_experiment_variants (
    experiment_id       TEXT NOT NULL,
    variant_type        TEXT NOT NULL,   -- 'dataset'|'model_config'|'mcp_version'|'tool_variant'|'workflow_config'
    variant_id          TEXT NOT NULL,
    FOREIGN KEY (experiment_id) REFERENCES lab_experiments(experiment_id)
);

-- Runs (one per Cartesian product cell)
CREATE TABLE lab_runs (
    run_id              TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    experiment_id       TEXT NOT NULL,
    task_id             TEXT NOT NULL,
    model_config_id     TEXT NOT NULL,
    mcp_version_id      TEXT NOT NULL,
    tool_variant_id     TEXT,            -- nullable: no variant override
    workflow_config_id  TEXT NOT NULL,
    status              TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
                                         -- pending|running|completed|failed|timed_out|cancelled
    started_at          TEXT,
    completed_at        TEXT,
    FOREIGN KEY (experiment_id) REFERENCES lab_experiments(experiment_id)
);

-- Trace events for a run (sealed after run completes)
CREATE TABLE lab_trace_events (
    run_id      TEXT NOT NULL,
    seq         INTEGER NOT NULL,       -- 0-based, immutable
    event_type  TEXT NOT NULL,
    ts          TEXT NOT NULL,
    payload     BLOB NOT NULL,          -- JSON
    PRIMARY KEY (run_id, seq),
    FOREIGN KEY (run_id) REFERENCES lab_runs(run_id)
);

-- Sealed flag per run (once set, lab_trace_events for that run are immutable)
CREATE TABLE lab_trace_sealed (
    run_id      TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    sealed_at   TEXT NOT NULL,
    FOREIGN KEY (run_id) REFERENCES lab_runs(run_id)
);

-- Evaluation results (one per run)
CREATE TABLE lab_eval_results (
    run_id              TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    experiment_id       TEXT NOT NULL,
    classification      TEXT NOT NULL,  -- success|partial_success|failure|error
    tool_call_accuracy  REAL NOT NULL,
    latency_ms          REAL NOT NULL,
    total_tokens        INTEGER NOT NULL,
    estimated_cost_usd  REAL NOT NULL,
    turn_count          INTEGER NOT NULL,
    error_field         TEXT,           -- set when classification=error
    detail              BLOB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',   -- JSON, raw scorer output
    FOREIGN KEY (run_id) REFERENCES lab_runs(run_id),
    FOREIGN KEY (experiment_id) REFERENCES lab_experiments(experiment_id)
);

-- Baselines for regression detection
CREATE TABLE lab_baselines (
    baseline_id     TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    experiment_id   TEXT NOT NULL,
    dataset_id      TEXT NOT NULL,
    dataset_version INTEGER NOT NULL,
    variant_key     TEXT NOT NULL,      -- stable hash of variant combo
    set_at          TEXT NOT NULL,
    UNIQUE (dataset_id, dataset_version, variant_key),
    FOREIGN KEY (experiment_id) REFERENCES lab_experiments(experiment_id)
);

-- Regression reports
CREATE TABLE lab_regression_reports (
    report_id       TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    experiment_id   TEXT NOT NULL,
    baseline_id     TEXT NOT NULL,
    generated_at    TEXT NOT NULL,
    entries         BLOB NOT NULL,      -- JSON array of RegressionEntry
    FOREIGN KEY (experiment_id) REFERENCES lab_experiments(experiment_id),
    FOREIGN KEY (baseline_id) REFERENCES lab_baselines(baseline_id)
);

-- Mock MCP fixture sets
CREATE TABLE lab_mock_fixtures (
    fixture_id      TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    name            TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    fallback_mode   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'error',  -- 'error'|'empty'
    entries         BLOB NOT NULL,      -- JSON array of {tool_name, arg_hash, response}
    created_at      TEXT NOT NULL
);
```

**Indexes:**
```sql
CREATE INDEX idx_lab_runs_experiment ON lab_runs(experiment_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_lab_runs_status ON lab_runs(status);
CREATE INDEX idx_lab_trace_events_run ON lab_trace_events(run_id, seq);
CREATE INDEX idx_lab_eval_results_experiment ON lab_eval_results(experiment_id);
```

